!panic: fixedbugs2522acorrectjumpoutofahandlerthroughacopiedbufferisrefusedinwordsthatsayso.answer was called after C, inside a signal handler, jumped to a buffer this runtime never saw filled (copied with `memcpy`, or saved where it does not look), so whether the jump left the handler is not known: a handler not seen to end is held to be running, where neither this runtime's memory nor the C library's is safe to use. No function of the program is a signal handler: after `hero_net_catch_stop() -> i64` (`hero_net.h`), Ctrl-C, SIGTERM and `hero_net_ask_stop() -> ()` only make `hero_net_stop_asked() -> i64` answer 1 and a waiting call of that layer answer stopped; `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`) counts any other signal, and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` gives the count since its last call
